   "module_16730315758341": {
    "body": {
     "hs_enable_module_padding": true,
     "hs_wrapper_css": {
      "padding-bottom": "10px",
      "padding-left": "20px",
      "padding-right": "20px",
      "padding-top": "10px"
     },
     "html": "<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Hey {{ contact.firstname }},</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\">The GI tract is related to the health of multiple bodily functions, yet many people don't think to discuss it with their doctors. How often do you talk to your patients about their gut health?&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\">If your patients are experiencing bowel irregularity, frequent digestive discomfort, or even mood changes, chances are it can be traced back to the gut. Even if they don't always mention it first, starting a conversation about GI health can uncover new ways to support your patients.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Check out our article on GI tract health and our recommended supplements below. Use this information to connect with your patients and find new ways to support them!</span></p>",
     "module_id": 1155639
    },
